T1  SI: x,t -> lambda x, lambda t; fixed mass => rho_b -> lambda^-3 rho_b, d^3x -> lambda^3 d^3x, phi -> phi (+ const ln lambda)
    int |P|^n d^3x scales as lambda**(3 - n); invariant for all lambda iff n in [3]
    general W: Eq(lambda**3*W(p/lambda), W(p))  at lambda = p  ->  Eq(p**3*W(1), W(p))  =>  W(p) = W(1) p^3 (homogeneous degree 3)
    source int alpha rho_b phi d^3x scales as 1 (phi's additive ln(lambda) shift multiplies the fixed mass: no force)
    quadratic |grad phi - P/a|^2 = |D|^2/a^2: on-shell (Gauss fixes D) 1/lambda; off-shell lambda (a constraint term that enforces P = a grad phi in the deep regime); stiffness |grad P|^2: 1/lambda
    deep effective action on P = a grad phi: int beta a^3 |grad phi|^3/3 d^3x scales as 1 (the AQUAL deep form)
  [PASS] T1 SI forces the cubic: |P|^n invariant iff n = 3: True; general W homogeneous degree 3: True; source factor 1; quadratic on-shell 1/lambda, stiffness 1/lambda (irrelevant at large lambda)

T2  W = beta |P|^n / n, gamma = 0, point source: D = a beta p^(n-1) (from grad phi = P/a + beta p^(n-2) P), D = alpha M/(4 pi r^2)
    dlnV^2/dlnr = (n - 3)/(n - 1)  -> flat iff n in [3];  dlnV^4/dlnM = 2/(n - 1)  -> V^4 propto M iff n in [3]
    SI + G, a0 only as A0 = G a0 ([L^4 M^-1 T^-4]): V = A0^x M^y r^z with [V] = L T^-1  ->  [{x: 1/4, y: 1/4, z: 0}]  (unique; no r dependence)
    deep law g = sqrt(A0 M)/r: g(lambda r) / (g(r)/lambda) = 1;  Newton: 1/lambda
